Z||000006||rockcrawl||10-01-2000||09:20 AM||||Haze, If you go back and read the description for the first auction, the guy clearly states that the car has a salvage title, and explains why. In the second one, the guy pretty much says your not going to be able to drive it home, and from the description, it seems like he's being pretty honest about the condition of the car. The Carfax report doesn't show a salvege title, just minor accidents. How many Fieros are out there that haven't been bumped once or twice? Besides, check out that price for an 88 Formula, do you expect it to be perfect?<P>Fieros are getting old, who cares if they have a salvage title or not (although it should be disclosed at time of sale), I have three with salvage titles, and two of them are the absolute nicest Fieros I've ever owned (out of 10).<P>Anyway, the point of my post... I think both of those sellers are being honest about the cars they are selling. The first guy just forgot to check the box for salvage title when he posted. Remember, they haven't owned the car since new, and if they don't have access to carfax, they have no idea (nor should they care) about it's history. They are just presenting the car as it is.  <P>Flame Suit......ON<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||10-01-2000||11:53 AM||||The wording on the first one is flaky. he says it's clean in on sentance then tells why it has a salvage tittle.<P>The other one indicates all kinds of problems. so stuff on car fax isn't a big suprise.<P>If you feel they are a rip then you can forward the reports to Ebay will close them if they see a problem. Ebay is under big pressure from the FTC to prevent fraud because of a high volume of complaints. The FTC also has a place to file complaints online.<P><BR>thanks for the link. My car was so clean it squeeked. My van didn't have any big suprises. (odo over limit. I knew that.)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Babygirl||10-01-2000||01:16 PM||||Thanks for the link Haze!  I just ran mine and she came out perfect!  Never ever had a problem title issued!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I wasn't really concerned, but then again, I've only had her a month.  Thanks again!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||6
Z||000009||rockcrawl||10-01-2000||03:22 PM||||Ogre,<BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>The wording on the first one is flaky. he says it's clean in on sentance then tells why it has a salvage tittle<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I've got an '87 GT with a salvege title. The interior is nearly flawless except for the headliner. The engine is so clean you could eat off it.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
