Z||000016||Songman||10-05-2000||01:20 AM||||Very strange! Tried it several times with title in hand and same thing each time... The VIN looks similar to the number on my other 88...<P>Formula - 1G2PE1194JP202775<BR>Coupe - 1G2PE11R4JP205756<P>The only major difference is the 8th digit which I assume is the engine code. I ran the coupe number through and it worked fine. Still get this message for the Formula: Carfax© has no data on your VIN<BR>Carfax has no data available on the VIN you supplied, "1G2PE1194JP202775."<P>Should I be worried? I have the title and a car that matches? Hmmmmm...||||reg||1
Z||000017||RossT||10-05-2000||01:44 AM||||I just ran your VIN thru <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.net</A>  vin decoder and had no problems decoding.  I don't know what to tell you.  Could be that the sate (s) were it has been registered may not report to carfax, or whatever central collection agency that they use.<P>I wouldn't worry about it.  If you still are I would check with your insurance company.  The will be able to tell you something about the history.  Its in their best interest.<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 10-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||mrfiero||10-05-2000||09:47 AM||||Songman,<P>You're not the only one having trouble pulling up a VIN.  I searched all of my current and most recent Fieros ( about a dozen) and all came back with some info.<P>I tried running my very first Fieros VIN and it came back with no data  available.  I bought this '88 GT back in 1990 and it was totalled in 1995......I don't know why there isn't any info available on it.  Here's the VIN:  1G2PG1190JP231007<P>I just think some VINs slipped through the cracks at car fax (hey, that rhymes!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
